        "cap": "A girl hugs her loyal dog; hearts float above them."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>cred</b> = <b>believe</b>. <b>fid</b> = <b>trust, faith</b>. <b>ver</b> = <b>true</b>. <b>sci</b> = <b>know</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "Watch the endings, because they change the meaning a lot. <b>credible</b> (<i>-ible</i>, able to be) means believable. <b>credulous</b> (<i>-ulous</i>, inclined to) means too ready to believe. <b>incredulous</b> means not believing. <b>credence</b> (<i>-ence</i>, a noun) is belief itself."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "cred",
            "fid"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "cred (believe) and fid (trust)."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "ver",
            "sci"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "ver (true) and sci (know)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>credible</b><br>believable; worthy of trust",
            "<b>cred</b> <i>believe</i> + -ible <i>able to be</i><br>→ “able to be believed”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>credulous</b><br>too ready to believe things; easily fooled",
            "<b>cred</b> <i>believe</i> + -ulous <i>inclined to</i><br>→ “inclined to believe”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>incredulous</b><br>unwilling or unable to believe something",
            "in- <i>not</i> + <b>cred</b> <i>believe</i> + -ulous <i>inclined to</i><br>→ “not inclined to believe”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>fidelity</b><br>faithfulness and loyalty; also, accuracy",
            "<b>fid</b> <i>faith</i> + -elity<br>→ “faithfulness”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>confidant</b><br>a trusted friend you can share secrets with",
            "con- <i>thoroughly</i> + <b>fid</b> <i>trust</i> + -ant<br>→ “one you trust fully”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>diffident</b><br>shy and lacking confidence in oneself",
            "dif- <i>not</i> + <b>fid</b> <i>trust</i> + -ent<br>→ “not trusting (oneself)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>veracity</b><br>truthfulness; accuracy",
            "<b>ver</b> <i>true</i> + -acity<br>→ “truthfulness”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>verify</b><br>to check that something is true",
            "<b>ver</b> <i>true</i> + -ify <i>to make</i><br>→ “to show to be true”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>omniscient</b><br>knowing everything",
            "omni- <i>all</i> + <b>sci</b> <i>know</i> + -ent<br>→ “all-knowing”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Two near opposites",
        "q": "Zoe believed every rumor she heard, but her brother Kai doubted everything. Which one is <b>credulous</b> and which is <b>incredulous</b>?",
        "steps": [
          "Both words have <b>cred</b> (believe) and <b>-ulous</b> (inclined to).",
          "<b>credulous</b>: inclined to believe, too ready to believe things.",
          "<b>incredulous</b>: <i>in-</i> (not) + inclined to believe, unwilling to believe."
        ],
        "a": "Zoe is credulous; Kai is incredulous."
      },
