      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "Missing a root when it shrinks or hides. <b>fid</b> shrinks inside <b>diffident</b> (<i>dif-</i> + <i>fid</i>: not trusting oneself), and <b>ver</b> hides in <b>verdict</b> (a true saying). And keep <b>credulous</b> (too ready to believe) and <b>incredulous</b> (unwilling to believe) apart: they are near opposites."
